{
  "$comment": "Everyday words in, closed-vocabulary tags out. Hand-written and committed, hashed into every ReferenceMatchSet as lexicon_sha256 so an answer can be traced to the exact table that produced it. Two rules keep it honest. Every term is a value of InteractionTag, ContactTag or Posture in python/content_factory/schemas/reference.py, so a phrase can never expand to a tag no clip can carry. And a phrase never swallows a body-part word that still carries meaning on its own: 'head on shoulder' is a phrase, 'head on his shoulder' deliberately is not, so in a real sentence the bare 'shoulder' survives and still finds the shoulder material. Six interaction terms (head_on_shoulder, cuddle, slow_dance, carry_child, stroke_hair, hold_face) are in ABSENT_INTERACTIONS and match nothing on disk: they are mapped anyway so a query naming them comes back with the gap named rather than with a near miss. Entries are sorted by phrase and their targets are sorted, deduped and validated at load time.",
